    "commit_message": "Emergency Alert Hub: surface unknown-severity in heartbeats; sane refresh cadence\n\n1. Unknown-severity visibility (Captain: \"how do we stop these cropping\n   in every time\"): the orchestrator now counts unknown-severity alerts\n   per run and includes it in the heartbeat detail\n   (\"N alert(s), N unknown severity, N expired\"), and the workbench's\n   Source Health panel now always shows that detail text (was previously\n   hidden on 'ok' status) \u2014 a leak like HAYBOROUGH (caught by eyeballing\n   the alert table) now shows up on every run without a manual audit.\n\n2. Refresh cadence (Captain: \"60sec is no doubt overkill\"): backend only\n   ingests every 15min, so 60s browser polling bought nothing. Now\n   self-schedules hourly refreshes 07:00-19:00 local and pauses entirely\n   19:00-07:00, waking exactly at 07:00 rather than waiting for the next\n   hourly tick after a quiet night.\n\nVicEmergency real-severity feed: searched again, confirmed via EMV's own\nsupport article \u2014 no public severity/CAP feed exists yet (\"hope to make\nthis available... following CAP-AU-STD\"), only the incidents-only\nendpoint already wired. Not fixable until EMV ships it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011Q88CdbAYk33hiVJ7zUWs8",
